### Create the PR

\`\`\`bash
# Stage changes
git add packages/zest/src/$COMPONENT_NAME/
git add packages/zest/src/index.ts
git add apps/zest-docs/stories/$COMPONENT_NAME.stories.tsx

# Commit with message
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
[TICKET-123] Add/Update ComponentName Zest component

[Brief description of changes]

🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
EOF
)"

# Push branch
git push -u origin feature/TICKET-123-slug

# Create PR using gh
gh pr create --title "[TICKET-123] Add/Update ComponentName" --body "[PR body from template above]"
\`\`\`

### PHASE 11: Monitor GH Actions

Now monitor the GH actions on the PR. Keep waiting until some action fails or all checks pass.

Common issues to fix automatically:
- **TypeScript errors**: Type mismatches, missing imports, incorrect prop types
- **Linting errors**: Prettier formatting, ESLint rule violations
- **Test failures**: Failing tests, outdated snapshots
- **Import path issues**: Incorrect import paths, circular dependencies

### Fix TypeScript Errors

\`\`\`bash
# Run TypeScript check locally
yarn tsc --noEmit

# Common fixes:
# - Add missing type imports
# - Fix prop type definitions
# - Add missing type exports to index.ts
\`\`\`

### Fix Linting Errors

\`\`\`bash
# Run Prettier
yarn prettier --write packages/zest/src/$COMPONENT_NAME/

# Run ESLint
yarn eslint --fix packages/zest/src/$COMPONENT_NAME/
\`\`\`

### Fix Test Failures

\`\`\`bash
# Run tests
yarn test ComponentName.test.tsx

# Update snapshots if UI changed intentionally
yarn test ComponentName.test.tsx -u

# Push fixes
git add .
git commit -m "fix: Address CI failures"
git push
\`\`\`

**CONTINUE MONITORING** until all checks are green.

**ONLY QUIT AND SUCCEED** when all the checks are green and the PR is ready for review.

## Report

**IF NEW COMPONENT**:
1. **Summary of what was created**:
   - Component name: ComponentName
   - Location: \`packages/zest/src/ComponentName/\`
   - Files created: [list all files]
   - Variants implemented: [list variants]
   - Sizes implemented: [list sizes]
   - Features: [list notable features]

2. **PR Information**:
   - PR link: [URL]
   - Branch: feature/TICKET-123-slug
   - Status: [All checks passing ✅ / Some checks failing ⚠️]
   - Preview link: [When available from GH Actions]

3. **Usage Example**:
   \`\`\`typescript
   import { ComponentName } from '@/libs/zest';

   <ComponentName
     variant="brand"
     size="md"
     onClick={handleClick}
     data-testid="my-component"
   >
     Content
   </ComponentName>
   \`\`\`

4. **Next Steps**:
   - Request review from the design system team
   - Once approved and merged, the component will be available in \`@/libs/zest\`
   - Update Zest documentation if needed
   - Announce new component to the team

**IF UPDATE EXISTING**:
1. **Summary of what was updated**:
   - Component: ComponentName
   - Location: \`packages/zest/src/ComponentName/\`
   - Changes made: [detailed list]
   - Breaking changes: [Yes/No, explain if yes]
   - Files modified: [list files]

2. **PR Information**:
   - PR link: [URL]
   - Branch: feature/TICKET-456-slug
   - Status: [All checks passing ✅ / Some checks failing ⚠️]
   - Preview link: [When available from GH Actions]

3. **Migration Guide** (if breaking changes):
   \`\`\`typescript
   // Before
   <ComponentName oldProp={value} />

   // After
   <ComponentName newProp={value} />
   \`\`\`

4. **Next Steps**:
   - Request review from the design system team
   - Once approved and merged, update any dependent code
   - Communicate breaking changes to affected teams
   - Update component documentation

**Success!** Your Zest component has been [added/updated] and is ready for review!

## Critical Rules

**DO:**
- Use design tokens for ALL styling (never hardcode colors, spacing, or typography)
- Use Zest primitives (Box, Text, Icon, etc.) for component structure
- Add data-testid to interactive elements for testing
- Add proper ARIA attributes for accessibility
- Follow the established patterns from \`ui-design-system-zest-components-web-patterns\` skill exactly
- Add Figma reference comments at the top of component files
- Wait for user confirmation at interactive phases

**DON'T:**
- Hardcode colors, spacing, or typography values
- Skip accessibility requirements (ARIA attributes, keyboard navigation)
- Create components without tests and Storybook documentation
- Deviate from established component file structure patterns
- Skip the Figma design analysis phase
- Push code without running tests first (when local testing is available)
"
`;
